I'm Richard I'm one of the producers on  cyberpunk I'm currently working closely  with the level design team and the 3d  assets team and when it came to  cyberpunk and switching from the fantasy  world from The Witcher to this well  world of the future and night city it  was easier due to the fact that many of  our people working with us are huge fans  of the tabletop they played it in the  childhood and they somewhat knew the  world our story team is basically fluent  in cyberpunk and it helped us in the  beginning when we started off with the  project and still helps us through the  production even right now obviously now  team knows what cyberpunk is he knows  the version of what we want to create  with it I mean when it comes to the  switch from TVP to fpp it wasn't really  this decision about a challenge it was a  narrative based decision because we  believe that the fpp camera will allow  us to immerse to play away more into the  story and the environment we are  creating obviously as well we have the  combat sequences which are heavy  shooting focused because of the world in  which niceties taken place and fpp as an  office choice when it comes to those  mechanics Knight city is a condensed  phase of you know heavy skyscrapers  large warehouses on the outskirts and  you have to hold what to quality aspect  which adds footprint sizes right because  you can have one skyscraper with a  footprint of 120 square meters but you  can have 10 floors of that playable so  when it comes to like denser packed  areas in the city like the city center  Watson Heywood  you have community there there if their  routines you can observe them you can  interact with them when it comes to  places where there are not much people  because well it's either too violent in  Pacifica or it's just not inhabited  enough less and sender Domingo you still  have this kind of city flare I mean you  are still feeling you're in the city you  have trash flying around and even if you  think that there is nothing going on  there is something going on you are  never safe tonight City especially when  it's very calm there is something off if  night city is formed and you know that  you have to prepare yourself  myphones we've actually said that night  city is the worst city to live in ever  eh even it was it was built in a bad way  it's just not nice little traffic jams  everywhere so when it comes to  environment yes we want to be as  impressive but when it comes to place  choice and this freedom the player has  he will always feel like the whole city  is open to him he can go wherever he  want at any given moment he can pursue  some many activities on the way and I we  think that this is how we should  approach the topic of creating a  believable world based on the tabletop  but on the other hand providing freedom  to the player I don't want to overuse  this too much but you never know what  might happen and this feeling which will  always be with the player should make  him think about exactly about what he is  doing because everything could have  consequences  we as a player will have the freedom to  modify our body because this is how  cyberpunk works you are doing things to  yourself in order to augment yourself in  order to survive in this very hostile  environment which you are currently in  and therefore certainly the player  himself will come to some ideas and  start thinking that maybe this is a bit  too weird maybe I'll would I do this to  myself if I would be in the game so I  want certainly this topic will be  you know people will be made to think  about it naturally
 

